lazysite (0.9.0-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * EDGE channel: cut to edge first (BREAKING changes + a manager-UI save-path
    migration that must bed in before promotion to stable).
  * FIX/SM042: the Config page silently dropped settings (incl. the new service
    killswitches) - it saved through a legacy processor-as-pseudo-plugin path
    that ignored keys outside that schema. The whole site-settings page now
    loads via config-read and saves each key via config-set; the pseudo-plugin
    schema is retired and a parity guarantee test (t/lint/18) prevents the drift
    recurring.
  * BREAKING: every remote surface is now OFF by default and must be enabled in
    Site settings -> Services (or lazysite.conf): mcp_enabled, oauth_enabled,
    control_api_enabled, token_exchange_enabled = enabled. WebDAV nav/form-config
    editing now needs manage_nav / manage_forms (not manage_config). Agent
    feedback over MCP is now the `feedback` capability (off by default). The
    manager UI, page render, and content/theme/layout grants are unaffected.
  * SECURITY: service killswitches. MCP, OAuth, the control-API token path and
    token exchange each gain a conf killswitch (default off), read through one
    shared helper; a disabled surface refuses before doing any work and discloses
    nothing. Toggles surfaced in the Services section of the config page.
  * SECURITY: cross-plane capability consistency. WebDAV nav.conf -> manage_nav,
    form configs -> manage_forms (was manage_config, matching API/MCP);
    site-backup-create/upload/apply POST-forced (CSRF gap); WebDAV drift-guard
    test; in-tool actor backstop for the users tool's group/cap-mutating verbs.
  * SECURITY/FIX: SM127 token-path regression (reported on 0.8.0). The
    manager-UI-remote gate wrongly refused introspection (whoami /
    describe-capabilities) for any manager-linked account, and refused agent
    accounts (an account with the manager `ui` capability from a group but
    interactive login disabled, ui:false) despite them holding api/mcp + the
    action capability. The gate now blocks only accounts that can actually use
    the interactive UI (manager_ui AND login enabled) and never blocks
    introspection. Fixed on both the control-API and MCP channels.
  * SECURITY: SSRF guard on domain-check. Its outbound TLS/HTTPS probes are
    refused unless every RESOLVED address is public (blocks loopback, RFC1918,
    169.254.169.254 metadata, CGNAT, IPv6 ULA/link-local; closes DNS rebinding
    and IP-literal/localhost). domain-preview unaffected.
  * Tenant-token isolation pinned by test (a token is per-site; it cannot
    authenticate against another site's docroot).

